-- title:
--   q-expansion isomorphism k⊗_ℤS₂(Γ₀(N),ℤ)≅ H⁰(Ω¹)
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, let $N\ge 1$ be an integer and assume that the image of $N$ in $k$ is nonzero. Write $F=$ `modularFunctionFieldC k N` for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $k((q))$ over $k$ generated by `jqModC k` and its $N$-fold $q$-substitution `jqNModC k N`, i.e. the subfield $k(j(q),j(q^N))\subseteq k((q))$. Let $L=$ [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) be the $\mathbb Z$-submodule of the space of weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ spanned by those forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19) are rational integers, and let `regularDifferentials k F` be the $k$-submodule of $\Omega_{F/k}$ consisting of those $\omega$ such that for every place $v$ of $F$ over $k$ (a proper valuation subring of $F$ containing $k$ whose ring is a principal ideal ring) one has $\omega=f\cdot\mathrm{d}t_v$ for some $f$ in that valuation subring, $t_v$ a uniformiser at $v$. The assertion is that there exists a $k$-linear isomorphism $e\colon k\otimes_{\mathbb Z}L\to$ `regularDifferentials k F` such that for all $c\in k$, $f\in L$ and $a\colon\mathbb N\to\mathbb Z$ with $\mathrm{qCoeff}(f)(n)=a_n$ for all $n$, the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{qExpansionDiffAlong}$ of $e(c\otimes f)$ along the inclusion $F\subseteq k((q))$ — the $k$-linear map sending $\mathrm{d}x$ to $q\,\mathrm{d}x/\mathrm{d}q$ and satisfying $\varphi(f\omega)=f\varphi(\omega)$ — equals $c\sum_{n}\bar a_n q^n$, the reduction in $k$ of the Fourier expansion of $f$.
--
--   This is the comparison, over any algebraically closed field in which $N$ is invertible, between integral weight-two cusp forms on $\Gamma_0(N)$ reduced to $k$ and regular differentials on the modular curve, normalised by $q$-expansions; since pure tensors span the source, the stated compatibility pins $e$ down. It combines the existence of a regular differential with prescribed reduced $q$-expansion with the equality of $\dim_k H^0(\Omega^1)$, the genus of $X_0(N)$ and the rank of the integral cusp-form lattice, and is used in bounding the rank of torsion in differentials via [`ModularCurve.finrank_mTorsionDiffOf_le_finrank_of_adjoin_range_eq_top`](thm.html#ModularCurve.finrank_mTorsionDiffOf_le_finrank_of_adjoin_range_eq_top).
